WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:01:02.350 --> 00:01:05.970
Something is happening in Israel.

00:01:05.970 --> 00:01:15.409
I don’t think it would be an understatement
to say that the State of Israel has been in

00:01:15.409 --> 00:01:17.360
the spotlight since it was founded in 1948.

00:01:17.360 --> 00:01:23.149
We’re talking about 70 years of wars with
their Arab neighbors; seven decades of severe

00:01:23.149 --> 00:01:26.060
tensions due to the Palestinian situation.

00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:31.810
70 years of international isolation only mitigated
by the strong support of the United States.

00:01:31.810 --> 00:01:36.350
But hold on, because now all that is changing.

00:01:36.350 --> 00:01:50.179
In recent years, Israel has gone from being
as vilified as Lindsey Lohan to being as exalted

00:01:50.179 --> 00:01:51.179
as Natalie Portman.

00:01:51.179 --> 00:01:52.860
You think I'm exaggerating, right?

00:01:52.860 --> 00:01:58.600
Well, take a look at what 2018’s number
one villain had to say about the country.

00:01:58.600 --> 00:02:01.950
Saudi Prince Says Israelis Have Right to ‘Their
Own Land’ NYTimes)

00:02:01.950 --> 00:02:08.700
The turnaround is so dramatic that the Israeli
national anthem has made it to - wait for

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:15.060
it - Abu Dhabi.

00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:16.060
See for yourself.

00:02:16.060 --> 00:02:20.870
In October 2018, at the medal ceremony of
an international judo tournament in Abu Dhabi,

00:02:20.870 --> 00:02:26.170
the Israeli national anthem was played for
the first time ever in the United Arab Emirates.

00:02:26.170 --> 00:02:31.010
The woman you see crying emotionally is the
Israeli Minister of Culture and Sports, Miri

00:02:31.010 --> 00:02:34.370
Regev, a former Brigadier General in the 2006
Lebanon War.

00:02:34.370 --> 00:02:36.730
A bit of an about-face huh?

00:02:36.730 --> 00:02:41.680
Especially if we take into account that to
this day not one country in the Arabian peninsula

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:44.060
officially recognizes Israel as a State.

00:02:44.060 --> 00:02:52.870
But that’s not the end of it.

00:02:52.870 --> 00:02:56.790
Around the same time, the Israeli Prime Minister
himself, Benjamin Netanyahu, made a secret

00:02:56.790 --> 00:02:58.230
visit to the Sultan of Oman.

00:02:58.230 --> 00:03:02.959
And, in the past few months, several Israeli
ministers have visited the Dubai emirate and

00:03:02.959 --> 00:03:06.330
have even met with Qatari representatives.

00:03:06.330 --> 00:03:10.600
You heard that correctly.

00:03:10.600 --> 00:03:16.030
So how on earth did Israel achieve such diplomatic
advances in such a short time?

00:03:16.030 --> 00:03:17.949
What do the Palestinians think of all this?

00:03:17.949 --> 00:03:20.410
And perhaps the most important question of
all:

00:03:20.410 --> 00:03:25.780
Is an enduring, peaceful resolution finally
in sight for this region that has spent decades

00:03:25.780 --> 00:03:27.720
as the planet’s powder keg?

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:31.250
Today, in VisualPolitik, we’ll answer all
these questions, but first, let’s rewind

00:03:31.250 --> 00:03:41.639
for a bit of History.

00:03:41.639 --> 00:03:42.900
Listen up.

00:03:42.900 --> 00:03:44.780
(A DIFFICULT BIRTH)

00:03:44.780 --> 00:03:46.660
May 14th, 1948.

00:03:46.660 --> 00:03:49.959
Ben Gurion proclaims the independence of the
State of Israel.

00:03:49.959 --> 00:03:55.100
The very next day, this brand new nation is
invaded by the armies of five Arab countries.

00:03:55.100 --> 00:03:59.479
But...why was there such a rapid and dramatic
reaction??

00:03:59.479 --> 00:04:06.419
Well, it turns out that since the late 1800s,
Jews had been buying up land in Palestine,

00:04:06.419 --> 00:04:09.180
which, at that time, was under the control
of the Ottoman Empire.

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:13.790
In the late nineteenth century, anti-Semitism
was running rife in Europe, so more and more

00:04:13.790 --> 00:04:17.480
Jewish people were emigrating to the traditional
land of their ancestors.

00:04:17.480 --> 00:04:21.949
After the First World War, however, Palestine
was put under a mandate leaving the running

00:04:21.949 --> 00:04:26.350
of the country in the hands of the UK.

00:04:26.350 --> 00:04:27.520
Problem sorted then?

00:04:27.520 --> 00:04:28.520
Not exactly.

00:04:28.520 --> 00:04:32.500
If the British put forward policies favouring
the Jews, the Arabs reacted with riots and

00:04:32.500 --> 00:04:34.480
protests of all kinds.

00:04:34.480 --> 00:04:37.700
On the other hand, if any British measure
favoured Arab interests, Jewish armed groups

00:04:37.700 --> 00:04:44.729
leapt into action.

00:04:44.729 --> 00:04:47.400
Twenty years later, World War II further complicated
the situation.

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:51.690
As you can imagine, the Jewish exodus to Palestine
only increased in the wake of the horrors

00:04:51.690 --> 00:04:52.690
of the Holocaust.

00:04:52.690 --> 00:05:05.810
What’s more, it highlighted the need for
a dedicated Jewish state.

00:05:05.810 --> 00:05:09.910
Meanwhile in Palestine, the situation became
increasingly unsustainable.

00:05:09.910 --> 00:05:14.510
Overwhelmed by events, the British authorities
handed control over to the United Nations.

00:05:14.510 --> 00:05:18.680
And that chain of events brought about one
of the most contentious resolutions in the

00:05:18.680 --> 00:05:23.570
history of the United Nations: Resolution
181.

00:05:23.570 --> 00:05:29.750
With this resolution, the UN proposed dividing
Palestine into two states.

00:05:29.750 --> 00:05:34.180
The first of roughly 14,000 square kilometres
would be controlled by a Hebrew Government

00:05:34.180 --> 00:05:38.790
with a Jewish population of around 60% but
the remaining 40% would be Arab.

00:05:38.790 --> 00:05:43.540
The second, slightly smaller state of around
11,000 kilometres would be controlled by the

00:05:43.540 --> 00:05:46.100
Palestinian people, with a Jewish population
of barely 2%.

00:05:46.100 --> 00:05:51.010
At the same time Jerusalem, Bethlehem and
the Holy Lands would be placed under an international

00:05:51.010 --> 00:05:54.000
mandate.

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:55.710
The Jews accepted the resolution.

00:05:55.710 --> 00:05:56.790
The Arabs did not.

00:05:56.790 --> 00:06:01.590
That’s why, the day after the proclamation
of Israel's independence in 1948, the country

00:06:01.590 --> 00:06:05.440
was invaded by Egypt, Syria, Lebanon, Iraq
and Jordan.

00:06:05.440 --> 00:06:09.820
And with that began a conflict that’s dragged
out over the past seven decades.

00:06:09.820 --> 00:06:18.870
As it happened, Israel, despite being a fledgling
nation and facing the armies of five different

00:06:18.870 --> 00:06:19.889
countries, was the clear victor..

00:06:19.889 --> 00:06:23.420
And this victory allowed Israel to expand
its territory considerably.

00:06:23.420 --> 00:06:27.750
It was also the first victory of the newly
created Israel Defense Forces, which went

00:06:27.750 --> 00:06:31.830
on to become one of the most powerful armies
in the world today.

00:06:31.830 --> 00:06:36.550
But this wouldn’t be the only war between
Israel and the Arab countries.

00:06:36.550 --> 00:06:38.530
Far from it..

00:06:38.530 --> 00:06:45.650
In 1967 the so-called 6-day war took place,
during which Israel took control of the Golan

00:06:45.650 --> 00:06:55.030
Heights, East Jerusalem, the West Bank, the
Gaza Strip and the Sinai Peninsula.

00:06:55.030 --> 00:06:56.560
Just six days.

00:06:56.560 --> 00:07:06.360
It was such a humiliating defeat for the Arab
countries that they spent time planning their

00:07:06.360 --> 00:07:12.470
revenge.

00:07:12.470 --> 00:07:16.580
Six years later, during the Yom Kippur Jewish
holiday, Israel was attacked by the Egyptian

00:07:16.580 --> 00:07:17.770
and Syrian armies.

00:07:17.770 --> 00:07:22.300
This time the war didn’t last 6 days but
19, and the result was practically the same:

00:07:22.300 --> 00:07:43.390
A clear and rapid victory for the Israeli
army.

00:07:43.390 --> 00:07:48.050
It was possibly as a result of this war that
the Egyptian President, Anwar al-Sadat, made

00:07:48.050 --> 00:07:50.210
one of his most famous statements:

00:07:50.210 --> 00:07:54.740
(“Russians can give you arms but only the
United States can give you a solution”.

00:07:54.740 --> 00:07:57.169
Anwar al-Sadat, Egyptian President.)

00:07:57.169 --> 00:08:07.740
(SADAT TAKES THE FIRST SHOT)

00:08:07.740 --> 00:08:14.650
1978 marked a turning point in Israel's relationship
with its neighbors.

00:08:14.650 --> 00:08:18.870
The Egyptian president, Anwar al-Sadat traveled
to Jerusalem, recognized the existence of

00:08:18.870 --> 00:08:30.199
Israel as a State before the Hebrew Parliament
and got ready to negotiate a Peace Treaty.

00:08:30.199 --> 00:09:05.649
That’s how, with 
a

00:09:05.649 --> 00:09:09.670
little mediation from Jimmy Carter, the Camp
David Agreements were forged.

00:09:09.670 --> 00:09:13.630
Israel returned the Sinai Peninsula to Egypt
and, Egypt became the first Arab country to

00:09:13.630 --> 00:09:37.779
have diplomatic relations with the Jewish
state.

00:09:37.779 --> 00:09:42.139
While Sadat may have taken the crucial first
step, he paid a very high price for it.

00:09:42.139 --> 00:09:45.279
Just three years later he was assassinated
by Islamic radicals.

00:09:45.279 --> 00:09:48.149
Even so, Egypt stuck to the terms of the Camp
David agreements.

00:09:48.149 --> 00:09:51.579
Now, you may be wondering, what was the outcome
of these agreements for Israel?

00:09:51.579 --> 00:09:55.069
Well basically two things happened:
Firstly, Jewish settlements began to emerge

00:09:55.069 --> 00:09:59.619
in the West Bank and Gaza This continues to
be a sticking point and one of the main obstacles

00:09:59.619 --> 00:10:01.399
to peace between the neighbouring states.

00:10:01.399 --> 00:10:06.809
Secondly there was a huge increase in violence
and terrorist attacks as Hezbollah and the

00:10:06.809 --> 00:10:10.459
Palestinian Liberation Organization, under
Yasir Arafat’s leadership, gathered force.

00:10:10.459 --> 00:10:15.699
At this time both organizations were operating
out of Lebanon which led to Israeli military

00:10:15.699 --> 00:10:18.749
intervention in that country on two occasions.

00:10:18.749 --> 00:10:23.110
The Arab-Israeli conflict did not let up.

00:10:23.110 --> 00:10:27.009
Despite the conflicts, Jordan also recognized
the Jewish state in the 1990s.

00:10:27.009 --> 00:10:30.160
This was during the time of the Madrid and
Oslo negotiations

00:10:30.160 --> 00:10:33.009
where, progress was made towards Palestinian
self-government.

00:10:33.009 --> 00:10:36.899
Up until that point, Palestine’s power to
make and implement its own policies had been

00:10:36.899 --> 00:10:38.399
very limited in practice.

00:10:38.399 --> 00:10:43.240
That may explain the years of prolonged tension
and be the reason the conflict is yet to come

00:10:43.240 --> 00:10:45.440
to a satisfactory resolution.

00:10:45.440 --> 00:10:57.870
However, as we told you at the beginning of
the video, now everything seems to be changing.

00:10:57.870 --> 00:11:07.699
(COLD WAR IN A HOT REGION)
To those who usually follow VisualPolitik,

00:11:07.699 --> 00:11:12.040
this may not surprise you:
The Middle East is experiencing its own version

00:11:12.040 --> 00:11:13.040
of a cold war.

00:11:13.040 --> 00:11:16.279
The clash between Riyadh and Tehran has reached
an unprecedented level.

00:11:16.279 --> 00:11:21.300
This Cold War has intensified since the end
of 2017 when Saudi Arabia, the Arab Emirates,

00:11:21.300 --> 00:11:25.920
Bahrain and Egypt imposed an almost total
economic blockade on Qatar because of its

00:11:25.920 --> 00:11:29.769
relations with Iran... and also for its support
of the Muslim Brotherhood.

00:11:29.769 --> 00:11:33.160
Which incidentally, is very closely linked
to Hamas in Palestine.

00:11:33.160 --> 00:11:38.029
Hamas, in turn, maintains very close relations
with Qatar

00:11:38.029 --> 00:11:42.139
Hamas Pays Gaza Clerks After Receiving $15
Million From Qatar.

00:11:42.139 --> 00:11:48.399
But, nowadays in the Middle East, having good
relations with Qatar can cost one dearly:

00:11:48.399 --> 00:11:53.220
Egypt court sentences Mursi to 25 years in
Qatar spy case.

00:11:53.220 --> 00:11:54.399
Wait, Eqypt?

00:11:54.399 --> 00:11:59.389
Qatar?, you’re probably thinking, “Simon,
What on earth does all this have to do with

00:11:59.389 --> 00:12:00.439
Israel?”

00:12:00.439 --> 00:12:06.529
Well, the fact is that this Arab Cold War
provides Israel with a unique opportunity..

00:12:06.529 --> 00:12:15.300
Let’s break it down..

00:12:15.300 --> 00:12:18.339
Israel is a declared enemy of Iran... and
vice versa.

00:12:18.339 --> 00:12:21.040
For Jerusalem, the Ayatollahs’ government
is their archenemy.

00:12:21.040 --> 00:12:23.020
And... you know the old saying…

00:12:23.020 --> 00:12:25.480
“My enemy's enemy is my friend”)

00:12:25.480 --> 00:12:26.540
So that means...

00:12:26.540 --> 00:12:33.439
Suddenly Israel has become a potential ally
for Ryad, a very important ally.

00:12:33.439 --> 00:12:41.449
And there’s more.

00:12:41.449 --> 00:12:46.279
The Arab countries want Washington's support
at all costs; so here’s a question:

00:12:46.279 --> 00:12:49.990
What would please the White House more than
Arab nations becoming close to the Jewish

00:12:49.990 --> 00:12:50.990
state?

00:12:50.990 --> 00:12:52.069
It's a no-brainer right?

00:12:52.069 --> 00:12:56.429
And, if we add to all this the fact that many
Arab capitals are getting tired of Palestine

00:12:56.429 --> 00:12:59.920
and of Hamas' ties with Qatar, then it looks
like a done deal.

00:12:59.920 --> 00:13:04.079
That’s why, when Australia suddenly announced
that it recognized Jerusalem as the Israeli

00:13:04.079 --> 00:13:09.230
capital, we saw reactions like this:

00:13:09.230 --> 00:13:12.930
Bahrain FM defends Australia's decision on
Jerusalem.

00:13:12.930 --> 00:13:14.240
Aljazeera)
But hold on.

00:13:14.240 --> 00:13:17.269
Don’t think that this is just about geopolitics.

00:13:17.269 --> 00:13:20.279
On this occasion, money also plays a key role.

00:13:20.279 --> 00:13:24.310
Let’s take a look.

00:13:24.310 --> 00:13:29.709
(BUSINESS AS USUAL)

00:13:29.709 --> 00:13:34.889
We’ve mentioned this in several videos:
Over the last two decades, Israel's economy

00:13:34.889 --> 00:13:38.189
has skyrocketed.

00:13:38.189 --> 00:13:45.149
The country has become a world leader in technological
innovation and now, to top it all off, it

00:13:45.149 --> 00:13:48.420
has discovered huge deposits of natural gas
off its coast.

00:13:48.420 --> 00:13:54.860
So now we see headlines like this:
Egyptian firm to buy $15 billion of Israeli

00:13:54.860 --> 00:13:55.860
natural gas.

00:13:55.860 --> 00:13:56.860
Reuters)
Whoa!

00:13:56.860 --> 00:14:00.740
We’re talking about the most significant
economic agreement ever achieved between these

00:14:00.740 --> 00:14:03.560
two countries.

00:14:03.560 --> 00:14:07.920
But Israel's economic ties with the Arab world
go much further than that.

00:14:07.920 --> 00:14:11.770
You see, while the Gulf countries may not
officially recognize the Israeli State, they

00:14:11.770 --> 00:14:20.220
do recognize their technological superiority,
especially in the areas of Defense and Security.

00:14:20.220 --> 00:14:22.129
And this has far-reaching consequences.

00:14:22.129 --> 00:14:27.399
In the midst of the Arab Cold War, Israeli
technology has become highly prized.

00:14:27.399 --> 00:14:31.579
So much so that there are strong indications
that Israel is already supplying technological

00:14:31.579 --> 00:14:35.839
equipment to Saudi Arabia, while the Saudi
secret services are sharing information with

00:14:35.839 --> 00:14:40.910
the Israeli intelligence agency Mossad.

00:14:40.910 --> 00:14:44.769
Relations seem to be so good that, according
to US sources, Saudi Arabia may have bought

00:14:44.769 --> 00:14:49.070
part of the Israeli missile defense system
technology known as the "Iron Dome".

00:14:49.070 --> 00:14:52.189
To be fair, Israel has denied it... but you
know that, in business, discretion rules.

00:14:52.189 --> 00:14:53.899
Especially on this occasion

00:14:53.899 --> 00:15:00.010
“There is an alignment of Israel and other
countries in the Middle East that would have

00:15:00.010 --> 00:15:02.179
been unimaginable 10 years ago.

00:15:02.179 --> 00:15:06.879
Certainly in my life time, I never saw anything
like it and I'm the same age as the State

00:15:06.879 --> 00:15:09.970
of Israel more or less, so it's an extraordinary
thing”.

00:15:09.970 --> 00:15:18.489
Benjamin Netanyahu.)

00:15:18.489 --> 00:15:22.189
These days, visits from the highest Israeli
authorities to many Arab countries are turning

00:15:22.189 --> 00:15:26.329
into a common event; significant trade agreements
are being signed and the security and defense

00:15:26.329 --> 00:15:28.999
ties seen today are unprecedented.

00:15:28.999 --> 00:15:34.529
So Arab – Israeli relations seem to be getting
better and better... nods and winks between

00:15:34.529 --> 00:15:35.819
the main players are a regular event.

00:15:35.819 --> 00:15:39.690
One example would be the Saudi government’s
decision to allow commercial flights to Israel

00:15:39.690 --> 00:15:42.860
to cross Saudi airspace for the first time
in 70 years.

00:15:42.860 --> 00:15:48.230
Of course, all this has a downside.

00:15:48.230 --> 00:15:52.410
Dealing with democratic countries is not the
same as dealing with dictatorships that sometimes

00:15:52.410 --> 00:15:53.989
seem stuck in the Middle Ages.

00:15:53.989 --> 00:15:57.519
You may get nasty surprises like this:

00:15:57.519 --> 00:16:01.999
(Israeli Software Helped Saudis Spy on Khashoggi,
Lawsuit Says.

00:16:01.999 --> 00:16:04.420
Anyway, that's how things stand today.

00:16:04.420 --> 00:16:07.959
Everything points to the likelihood that the
Arab – Israeli conflict could soon become

00:16:07.959 --> 00:16:08.959
a thing of the past.

00:16:08.959 --> 00:16:14.060
The only question remaining is, will we see
a solution to the core Palestinian problem?

00:16:14.060 --> 00:16:18.500
So I really hope you enjoyed this video, please
hit like if you did, and don’t forget to

